hite ahead by 15.2, Opus 5.5 played E3 and lost 15.2 points, bringing the lead back to 0.0. The engine preferred F2. It was the first of three blunders that undid the lead built over the previous twenty-odd moves."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "After Black's E2 gave the lead straight back (-14.4), Opus 5.5 played F2 and lost another 16.7 points, putting the lead at +2.3 for Black. The engine wanted B2 here, a point that came up again two moves later."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "Black's C1 lost 18.9 points, the 14k's worst move, and sent the lead back to -16.5 in White's favour. The engine's choice was B2, the point Opus 5.5 was about to take."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "Opus 5.5 played B2, which lost 19.1 points, the worst move of the game, and the lead went from -16.5 to +2.6 for Black. The engine preferred A2, and Black took it next. White's lead never came back, and Black ended the game 12 points ahead."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "Opus 5.5's B1 lost 3.6 points and left the lead at +6.3. From here Black's lead grew from +6.3 to +12.2 by move 38. Most of the later moves lost almost nothing, so the game was already decided."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py prints groups and liberties and count.py does an area count of the current board, with open regions left uncounted. Neither tries candidate moves or plays anything forward, and the other commands only grep and edit CLAUDE.md and games.md notes.", "stop": false}}